From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] MMI: 128-bit HI/LO for the parallel multiply, divide and move instructions

What it broke:
  On the EE, HI and LO are 128 bits each: the context keeps bits 0-63 in
  hi/lo and bits 64-127 in hi1/lo1 (MULT1, DIV1, MFHI1 and MTLO1 already
  use them). The MMI instructions that read or write all of HI and LO
  were translated as if HI and LO were 32-bit registers:
  - PMTHI/PMTLO copied only the low word of rs; PMFHI/PMFLO only bits
    0-63; PMFHL read only bits 0-63 and its LW/UW/SLW/LH/SH forms were
    built from the wrong lanes (LW of HI=5, LO=0x8000 gave
    {0x5, 0x8000, ...} instead of {LO.w0, HI.w0, LO.w2, HI.w2}).
  - PMULTH, PMADDH, PMSUBH, PHMADH and PHMSBH added all eight products
    into one 64-bit sum, instead of keeping each product in its own word
    of HI/LO and leaving {LO.w0, HI.w0, LO.w2, HI.w2} in rd.
  - PMULTW, PMULTUW, PMADDW, PMSUBW and PMADDUW also summed the two lane
    products; PDIVW, PDIVUW and PDIVBW divided only lane 0; PMTHL.LW
    wrote only words 0 and 1.
  Protector of Earth runs PMULTH followed by PMFHL.UW 36 times (the
  fixed-point loops at 0x1b59d0-0x1b6400), which therefore got wrong
  values.

The changes:
  - ps2_runtime_macros.h: inline helpers ps2_mmi_<instruction>(ctx, ...)
    that load HI/LO as four 32-bit words each, follow PCSX2's interpreter
    (pcsx2/MMI.cpp) word for word, including the PMADDW/PMSUBW hardware
    quirks it models and PHMSBH's complemented odd product, and store
    them back. The old PS2_PMFHL_* macros are gone (nothing else used
    them).
  - mmi_translation_helpers.cpp: PMFHI, PMFLO, PMTHI, PMTLO, PMTHL.LW,
    PMFHL.*, PMULTH, PMADDH, PMSUBH, PHMADH, PHMSBH, PMULTW, PMULTUW,
    PMADDW, PMSUBW, PMADDUW, PDIVW, PDIVUW and PDIVBW call them.

How it was checked:
  New per-instruction cases (tests/instructions, findings/14 s.8), with
  expected values from PCSX2 MMI.cpp: PMFHL LW/UW/SLW/LH/SH, PMULTH,
  PMADDH, PMSUBH, PHMADH, PHMSBH, PMULTW, PMULTUW, PMADDW, PMSUBW,
  PMADDUW, PDIVW, PDIVUW, PDIVBW, PMTHI/PMFHI, PMTLO/PMFLO and PMTHL.LW:
  all failed before, all pass after. ps2xTest 454/454. The game's code
  regenerated: only its 36 PMULTH and 36 PMFHL.UW lines changed; it builds
  and reaches the first level.

